WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.725
Now the fun part. This is
BrightLeaf's real-world stock sheet.

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:10.023
It started as an Odoo export three
years ago and has been passed between

00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:14.550
five people since. You might
recognise some of these crimes.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:20.897
Merged title rows. Supplier
names merged across several rows.

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:27.757
Quantities like "145 boxes",
"approx 1,850" and "18

00:00:27.797 --> 00:00:34.309
urgent!!". "BL 1002" with a space
next to "BL-1002" with a dash.

00:00:34.922 --> 00:00:39.384
A blank SKU. Dates in
five different formats.

00:00:39.997 --> 00:00:42.384
Red cells only Tom understands.

00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:45.409
And a TOTAL row that just says "lots".

00:00:46.021 --> 00:00:47.722
A human can muddle through.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:50.334
An agent will stumble on every one.

00:00:50.947 --> 00:00:52.084
Let's fix them.

00:00:53.264 --> 00:00:57.337
Fix one: I delete the top three
rows: the merged title, the "prepared

00:00:57.377 --> 00:00:59.064
by" line and the blank row.

00:00:59.677 --> 00:01:01.527
Now row 1 is the headers.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.803
Fix two: merged cells.

00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:08.738
The supplier column looks tidy,
but only the top cell of a merge

00:01:08.778 --> 00:01:10.203
actually holds the name.

00:01:10.815 --> 00:01:14.613
The rows underneath are empty, so
if you sort or filter, products lose

00:01:14.653 --> 00:01:19.228
their supplier. Format,
Merge cells, Unmerge.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:23.440
See the blanks? I copy each name down.

00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:26.365
Every row now knows its own supplier.

00:01:27.548 --> 00:01:30.161
Fix three: inconsistent IDs.

00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:36.708
To a computer, "BL 1002" and "BL-1002"
are as different as "apple" and

00:01:36.748 --> 00:01:42.483
"banana". Edit, Find and replace,
"BL space" with "BL dash", Replace

00:01:42.523 --> 00:01:47.821
all. Then Data, Data cleanup, Trim
whitespace, to remove invisible

00:01:47.861 --> 00:01:51.346
spaces, the number one reason a
VLOOKUP says "not found" when you can

00:01:51.386 --> 00:01:52.936
see the value right there.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.860
Fix four: duplicates.

00:01:56.473 --> 00:02:00.923
Data, Data cleanup, Remove
duplicates, data has a header row.

00:02:01.535 --> 00:02:03.635
The duplicate hex bolts disappear.

00:02:04.248 --> 00:02:08.208
The two corrugated box rows had
different date formats, so I delete one

00:02:08.248 --> 00:02:14.120
by hand. Before this, a stock total
would have counted 2,360 boxes

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.008
instead of 1,180, which is above
the reorder point of 1,500, so the

00:02:20.048 --> 00:02:22.285
reorder alert would never have fired.

00:02:23.456 --> 00:02:25.856
Fix five: one fact per cell.

00:02:26.469 --> 00:02:29.381
I insert a Unit column
and split every quantity.

00:02:29.993 --> 00:02:34.618
"145 boxes" becomes 145 and "box".

00:02:35.231 --> 00:02:41.254
"approx 1,850" becomes 1,850,
with "estimate, recount" in the

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:47.679
remarks. And our stretch wrap: "21
cartons, 12 rolls each, plus 8 loose"

00:02:47.719 --> 00:02:51.993
becomes 260 rolls, because
the reorder point is in rolls.

00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:54.591
Not a stock-out. The

00:02:54.631 --> 00:02:56.904
eighteen-hundred-dollar
cell, fixed in five

00:02:56.944 --> 00:02:57.868
seconds.

00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:01.255
Fix six: the blank ID.

00:03:01.867 --> 00:03:04.155
The safety gloves have no SKU.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.717
The product list says BL-1004.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.480
A row without an ID is a
parcel without a label.

00:03:12.644 --> 00:03:16.479
Fix seven: the red cells meant
"urgent", so I write that in the remarks

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:17.832
and reset the colour.

00:03:18.444 --> 00:03:20.182
And the TOTAL row goes.

00:03:20.794 --> 00:03:24.854
Totals belong in reports, not data
tables, or the agent counts them as a

00:03:24.894 --> 00:03:25.657
product.

00:03:26.822 --> 00:03:32.285
Before and after. Messy: seventeen
rows and two red "urgent" cells.

00:03:32.897 --> 00:03:37.770
Clean: ten rows, one per product,
and four need reordering: boxes,

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:40.522
gloves, wheels and hydraulic oil.

00:03:41.135 --> 00:03:45.235
Two surprises. The packing
tape coloured red for "urgent"?

00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:50.447
1,850 rolls against a
reorder point of 1,000.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.457
Fine. And the hydraulic oil nobody
flagged is at 31 drums against 40,

00:03:56.497 --> 00:03:59.110
with a 14-day lead time from Dubai.

00:03:59.722 --> 00:04:03.195
That's a real emergency, and the
messy sheet was hiding it under "check

00:04:03.235 --> 00:04:04.060
with Tom".
